00:15:39.220 --> 00:15:40.420
You've got to be out of your mind, lady.

00:15:40.740 --> 00:15:42.440
Do you hear how she talks to me?

00:15:43.660 --> 00:15:46.680
Bobby would never talk to me like that, would you, sweetheart?

00:15:46.940 --> 00:15:48.040
No, of course not.

00:15:48.440 --> 00:15:49.340
You're my mommy.

00:15:52.940 --> 00:15:53.620
That's sweet.

00:15:54.580 --> 00:15:56.500
You're going to make some man very happy one day.

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:05.000
Oh, boy. I thought you couldn't get to me this year, but, man, you are good.

00:16:05.520 --> 00:16:09.020
Is this still about me missing your show, Natalie? Is that it?

00:16:09.140 --> 00:16:11.320
Because I've seen it plenty of times.

00:16:11.480 --> 00:16:14.280
Oh, really? You have, huh? Name one time.

00:16:15.780 --> 00:16:18.340
I saw it when that little girl got a new heart.

00:16:19.630 --> 00:16:21.470
60 Minutes, and I was sitting right next to you.

00:16:22.150 --> 00:16:23.770
60 Minutes, that's a good show.

00:16:23.910 --> 00:16:27.810
See, now, if you were on 60 Minutes, I wouldn't forget to watch.

00:16:28.110 --> 00:16:29.830
I can't believe you.

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:36.610
If you'd have really done something with my life, I'd have sat her.

00:16:38.520 --> 00:16:39.680
I thought you'd leave that car.

00:16:40.380 --> 00:16:41.800
Okay, but I own the condo.

00:16:43.380 --> 00:16:45.920
Maybe one day I will be sitting next to Morley Safer.

00:16:46.400 --> 00:16:50.850
But until then, I am Natalie Jessica Caruso, gal on the go, and damn proud of it.

00:16:53.140 --> 00:16:54.280
Natalie, yeah?

00:16:56.560 --> 00:16:58.570
Are you having your period?

00:17:04.160 --> 00:17:05.720
He's going to be just fine.

00:17:05.800 --> 00:17:07.020
Oh, thank God.

00:17:07.320 --> 00:17:09.980
Now, we had to do a little stomach surgery on him,

00:17:09.980 --> 00:17:11.840
but if you follow this special diet,

00:17:12.040 --> 00:17:14.560
there's no reason he shouldn't have a complete recovery.

00:17:16.520 --> 00:17:25.500
I was not expecting that.

00:17:26.490 --> 00:17:27.030
Here you go.

00:17:28.520 --> 00:17:29.650
No, baby.

00:17:30.060 --> 00:17:30.940
Ooh, still stinky.

00:17:42.350 --> 00:17:43.870
Great cake, Mrs. Crusoe.

00:17:44.220 --> 00:17:46.840
Oh, you like that, do you, dear?

00:17:46.840 --> 00:17:49.260
Because it's not everyone's favorite.

00:17:51.530 --> 00:17:53.010
Open my other gift, Natalie.

00:17:54.180 --> 00:17:54.660
Okay, Dad.

00:18:02.910 --> 00:18:05.080
Oh, Dad, three, you see yours.

00:18:08.510 --> 00:18:10.170
Makes me wish I had more than one TV.

00:18:11.130 --> 00:18:12.490
What can I say?

00:18:13.120 --> 00:18:15.140
Your old man met his sales quota this month.

00:18:15.390 --> 00:18:16.490
Happy birthday, sweetheart.

00:18:16.710 --> 00:18:17.330
Thank you, Dad.

00:18:17.820 --> 00:18:20.540
You know, I don't think I know what it is you actually sell, Jack.

00:18:20.820 --> 00:18:22.360
Are you trying to be a smartass?

00:18:25.580 --> 00:18:28.300
Natalie, that gift over there is from me.

00:18:29.250 --> 00:18:29.590
Mom.

00:18:31.340 --> 00:18:32.660
I'm hanging by a thread here.

00:18:37.030 --> 00:18:41.500
And if I open that box, and it's another makeover gift certificate,

00:18:42.200 --> 00:18:44.410
I'm going to lose it.

00:18:44.630 --> 00:18:47.260
And if I go down, I'm taking you with it.

00:18:52.260 --> 00:18:54.620
I, uh, I gave her hangers.

00:18:56.300 --> 00:18:59.960
Derek, Natalie's father and I were watching the...

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:12.160
as folk on show I have been dying to ask you a couple of questions now where did I put that

00:19:12.160 --> 00:19:21.660
piece of paper you know hey that's okay really another time that show doesn't fool me all it is

00:19:21.660 --> 00:19:29.900
is a gay party of five I want you to open my present please Mary

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:32.780
Dad, could you hand Natalie that box?

00:19:33.020 --> 00:19:33.340
Sure.

00:19:40.140 --> 00:19:41.860
You mean to tell me that's not a limp?

00:19:44.820 --> 00:19:46.840
I'm getting used to Augie's hair like that.

00:19:47.380 --> 00:19:49.820
Yeah, um, is he okay?

00:19:50.990 --> 00:19:52.110
He's just tired.

00:19:52.230 --> 00:19:54.920
You should see him with the tennis ball.

00:19:56.550 --> 00:19:58.120
Oh, my gosh, Mom.

00:19:58.730 --> 00:19:59.510
Do you like it?

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:00.870
It's perfect.

00:20:01.540 --> 00:20:03.140
Look, everybody, it's me and Mom.

00:20:03.440 --> 00:20:06.440
It's from our weekend cruise to Ensenada.

00:20:07.060 --> 00:20:13.150
And I remember you saying that you wanted something to put on the end table in your condo, so...

00:20:13.430 --> 00:20:14.170
I did.

00:20:14.660 --> 00:20:16.820
Listen to me.

00:20:17.430 --> 00:20:19.430
Well, of course I did, sweetheart.

00:20:19.910 --> 00:20:21.770
I always listen to you.

00:20:22.340 --> 00:20:24.870
Now, give me a hug.

00:20:31.750 --> 00:20:32.330
Big Jack.

00:20:32.680 --> 00:20:33.760
Go start the coffee.

00:20:34.820 --> 00:20:36.260
I'm glad you came home for your birthday.

00:20:37.580 --> 00:20:38.340
Happy birthday, kitten.

00:20:38.630 --> 00:20:39.290
Thank you, Dad.

00:20:40.200 --> 00:20:40.900
You know what, Mom?

00:20:41.900 --> 00:20:43.600
I don't even care that you didn't make my favorite cake

00:20:43.600 --> 00:20:45.760
because that strawberry shortcake was delicious.

00:20:46.120 --> 00:20:47.460
Well, of course it was.

00:20:47.880 --> 00:20:51.760
I mean, who wants that crappy coconut cluster cake

00:20:51.760 --> 00:20:53.440
you're always asking for?

00:20:55.080 --> 00:20:59.200
No one eats it but you, and I'm not going to make it just for you.

00:21:04.120 --> 00:21:05.880
I'm going to go help Big Jack with coffee.

00:21:06.660 --> 00:21:12.550
We're going back to my place to drink tonight, aren't we?

00:21:12.810 --> 00:21:13.290
Oh, yeah.

00:21:13.370 --> 00:21:14.390
Mama needs a mudslide.

00:21:18.870 --> 00:21:20.370
Okay, here we go, Dante. Magic time.

00:21:21.130 --> 00:21:22.530
Hey, how you feeling today? Good?

00:21:22.670 --> 00:21:27.540
Yeah, me too.

00:21:30.860 --> 00:21:31.460
Okay, we all set?

00:21:32.970 --> 00:21:34.450
You got a hair sticking out of your nose.

00:21:34.650 --> 00:21:36.690
Ooh, big guy. You got my back in the nose.

00:21:38.470 --> 00:21:39.110
Am I good?

00:21:41.170 --> 00:21:47.610
So, Miss California, I'm Natalie Jessica Caruso,

00:21:47.630 --> 00:21:50.050
and welcome to another segment of Gal on the Go,

00:21:50.250 --> 00:21:51.710
where you give me two minutes,

00:21:51.730 --> 00:21:54.890
and I'll give you an educational, informational,

00:21:55.110 --> 00:21:56.970
and entertaining two minutes back.

00:21:58.640 --> 00:21:59.080
Today,

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:02.520
to the Happy Shepherd Planned Living Healthcare community

00:22:02.520 --> 00:22:03.820
for the aged and infirm.

00:22:04.020 --> 00:22:06.040
And what's on the activities calendar for today?

00:22:06.680 --> 00:22:07.140
Macrame?

00:22:07.670 --> 00:22:08.050
Bingo?

00:22:08.410 --> 00:22:10.450
Try suicide and clinical depression.

00:22:12.280 --> 00:22:12.660
Thank you.

00:22:12.760 --> 00:22:14.080
Excuse me, are these your sunglasses?

00:22:14.380 --> 00:22:15.340
Oh, thank you.

00:22:15.520 --> 00:22:17.660
Oh, I was going to kill myself if I didn't get these back.

00:22:17.820 --> 00:22:18.780
They're DKNY.

00:22:20.890 --> 00:22:21.910
D-K-N-Y.

00:22:23.350 --> 00:22:24.356
Thank you.

00:22:25.300 --> 00:22:27.280
Let's go cheer up some depressed seniors.
